BLOOD LIMS — Final demonstration release
Release: V12 Final Demo / GxP-oriented prototype  
Prepared: 2026-09-21
Scope
This release is frozen as the final classroom/demo version of the BLOOD LIMS Streamlit application. The UI is English-only to keep the workflow consistent and reduce the risk of partial translations.
Main controls included
CSV and HL7 v2 ORU^R01 file-based ingestion
Pre-validation before database write
Atomic batch import and source SHA-256
Import ledger and idempotent re-import protection
Technical validation followed by biological validation
Re-authenticated electronic signature
Critical / out-of-range classification
Controlled correction and void with supersession
Field-level audit metadata (old value, new value, reason, actor, timestamp)
Active-record-only exports after correction/supersession
Monthly VINC export restricted to REVIEWED + ACTIVE + cut-off
Package manifest and SHA-256
Internal mailbox delivery for free-tier demonstration
Weekly reminder, monthly VINC job, critical alert job
Anti-duplicate guards and automation run ledger
Optional patient PDF reporting after biological signature
SDTM LB/DM starter export and Define-XML starter
GitHub Actions CI for automated tests
Free Streamlit constraint
The application deliberately does not depend on a permanent server-side scheduler. Automation is evaluated on app load/wake and through a manual deterministic runner. This is a demonstration architecture, not a production-grade scheduled execution service.
